{
  "name": "Cluster",
  "package": "kernel",
  "description": "============================================================================\n Cluster State (cluster diagnostics, health, and metrics)\n ============================================================================\n\n Cluster is a state root that exposes cluster diagnostics and\n operational metrics. A background publisher in each node periodically\n computes metrics from JVM/Hazelcast APIs and writes them to the maps.\n Tacplus auto-generates Get/Set/Watch RPCs for each boundary.\n\n PATTERNS TO ADDRESS LATER:\n\n 1. Filtered queries: GetMapEntries needs key_prefix filter and limit.\n    The auto-generated collection Get doesn't support ad-hoc filtering.\n    Needs a hand-wrapped RPC or a new tacplus pattern for parameterized\n    queries on collections.\n\n 2. Transient point-in-time queries: ListLocks returns a snapshot of\n    lock state that changes too rapidly to publish to maps. Needs a\n    hand-wrapped RPC. Same applies to thread deadlock detection —\n    better as on-demand than periodic.\n\n 3. Publisher latency vs event-driven updates: Watch fires when maps\n    update, but the publisher writes on a fixed interval. For membership\n    changes, consider event-driven publishing (MembershipListener\n    triggers immediate cluster_info/cluster_health write) alongside\n    periodic publishing for metrics.",
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "cluster_info",
      "type": "message",
      "description": "cluster_info captures cluster membership, state, and version.\n Updated on membership change events and periodically.",
      "message": {
        "name": "AdminClusterInfo",
        "package": "hazelcast",
        "description": "AdminClusterInfo captures cluster membership, state, and version.",
        "fields": [
          {
            "name": "cluster_name",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "name": "state",
            "type": "string"
          },
          {
            "name": "members",
            "type": "message",
            "repeated": true,
